@startuml
title What a Malicious Specification Can and Cannot Do
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155

actor "adversary" as ADV #FCA5A5
rectangle "hostile spec value <latex>v^{\dagger}</latex>" as BAD #FEE2E2

package "Containment boundary" #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "**G1 — Shape gate**\n<latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> rejects any node whose tag\nis outside the closed elaborator set" as G1 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**G2 — Well-formedness gate**\n<latex>\texttt{validate\_language}</latex>, composition,\nauto-injection, stratification" as G2 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**G3 — Identity gate**\n<latex>\mathcal{F}(v^{\dagger}) \neq \mathcal{F}(v)</latex> for any honest <latex>v</latex>;\ntags become <latex>\texttt{GPrivate}(\texttt{mettail.term.}\mathcal{F}^{\dagger}\texttt{.}L)</latex>" as G3 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**G4 — Capability gate**\n<latex>\texttt{(\"handler\", }\mathit{urn}\texttt{)}</latex> resolves only against\n**already-registered** evaluators" as G4 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**G5 — Budget gate**\ncross-language fuel; guard metering;\nsaturation bounds <latex>\texttt{MAX\_ITERS}</latex>/<latex>\texttt{MAX\_NODES}</latex>" as G5 #DCFCE7
}

rectangle "victim language <latex>L</latex>\nterms and drivers under <latex>\mathcal{F}_L</latex>" as VICTIM #BFDBFE
rectangle "host Rholang state\n(names, RSpace data)" as HOST #BFDBFE

ADV --> BAD : authors and publishes
BAD --> G1
G1 --> G2 : shape OK
G2 --> G3 : well-formed
G3 --> G4
G4 --> G5

G1 -[#DC2626]-> ADV : **reject** unknown tag,\nbad arity, wrong scalar type
G2 -[#DC2626]-> ADV : **reject** undeclared category,\nnegation cycle, dangling label
G3 -[#DC2626]-> VICTIM : cannot forge <latex>\mathcal{F}_L</latex>;\npatterns simply never match
G4 -[#DC2626]-> ADV : unregistered URN <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> **inert**
G5 -[#DC2626]-> ADV : divergent theory <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> **starves itself**,\nnot the node

BAD -[#DC2626,dashed]-> HOST : **no path** — a spec is a value;\nelaboration performs no COMM and\ncreates no name

note bottom #FEF3C7
  **Residual risks, stated plainly.** (i) *Resource exhaustion at elaboration*: a spec is
  attacker-sized data, so <latex>|v|</latex> must be bounded before <latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> runs, and the WPDA/set-automaton
  build is superlinear in the rule count. (ii) *Namespace confusion*: two distinct languages
  may declare the same constructor **label**; only the fingerprint separates them, so any
  surface that resolves by bare name is unsafe. (iii) *A hostile spec is still a denial-of-service
  vector against its own installer* — install must be metered like any other deploy.
end note

legend right
  |= Color |= Role |
  |<#FEE2E2> | Attacker-supplied data |
  |<#DCFCE7> | Fail-closed gate |
  |<#BFDBFE> | Protected asset |
endlegend
@enduml
